{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionSU3RankSix","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionSU3RankSix","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionSU3Stabilizer","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivationsBound"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.finrank_su3_e1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.finrank_su3_e1","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionSU3RankSix.lean#L259-L263","doc":"**`dim 𝔰𝔲(3) = 8` unconditionally** at `e₁`: combine the `#3860` rank–nullity gate\n`finrank (su3 e) = 8 ↔ rank(evOct e) = 6` with `rank(evOct e₁) = 6`.  This is the\n`S⁶ = G₂/SU(3)` dimension count, fully in Lean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.finrank_range_evOct_e1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.finrank_range_evOct_e1","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionSU3RankSix.lean#L102-L257","doc":"**The rank of the color evaluation at `e₁` is 6** — `range(evOct e₁)` is the span of\nthe six images `±e₂, …, ±e₇`, an independent set.  Together with the `#3860` gate this\ncloses `finrank (su3 e₁) = 8 = dim SU(3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.range_evOct_eq_span_images","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.range_evOct_eq_span_images","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionSU3RankSix.lean#L74-L80","doc":"**`range(evOct e)` is the span of the 14 concrete image vectors** `evOct e (octDer i)`,\nbecause `octDer` spans `Der(𝕆)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.octDer_span_eq_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionDerivations.octDer_span_eq_top","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/OctonionSU3RankSix.lean#L34-L72","doc":"**The 14 explicit `𝔤₂` derivations span `Der(𝕆)`.** They are linearly independent\n(`octDer_linearIndependent`) and `dim Der(𝕆) = 14` (`octonion_derivation_dim`), so they\nform a basis. ","signatureChunk":0}]}